  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Marine Casualty and Pollution Database by the U.S. Coast Guard",
  "description": "Provides details about marine casualty and pollution incidents investigated by the U.S. Coast Guard Marine Safety Officer. Nationwide database containing information on marine pollution incidents, vessels casualties, vessel information and other matters containing information on these areas for incidents which occur on the Bering Sea and other parts of Alaska. The database is an invaluable source of information in understanding particulars and circumstances of marine accidents and pollution incidents. Source: Coast Guard Operations System Center - Martinsburg, West Virginia Referece: http://www.uscg.mil/hq/gm/index.htm\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Coast Guard record keeping and information analysis on marine pollution incidents, vessels casualties, vessel information and other matters containing information on these areas for incidents which occur on the Bering Sea and other parts of Alaska.",
